    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "Parasite: The organism that grows on the body of another organism and derives nutrients from it is known as a parasite. Examples of parasites are Cuscuta and orchids. Saprotroph: The organism that obtains nutrients from the dead or decaying organic matter is called saprotroph. Examples of saprotrophs are fungi and some bacteria.",
